What This Code Does
Think of this as a smart email assistant that helps companies respond to suppliers who are asking for price increases. Instead of a human reading the email and writing a response, this AI agent does it automatically.
Basic Structure Overview
1. Imports - Getting Tools Ready
pythonimport os
import logging
from datetime import datetime
# ... more imports
Think of imports like getting tools from a toolbox:

os - helps work with computer files and settings
logging - like keeping a diary of what the program does
datetime - handles dates and times
typing - helps make code clearer by saying what type of data we expect

2. Data Models - Organizing Information
pythonclass SupplierEmail(BaseModel):
    sender: EmailStr
    subject: str
    body: str
    # ... more fields
These are like templates or forms that organize information:

SupplierEmail: A form that stores email information (who sent it, subject, content)
JustificationAnalysis: A form that stores our analysis of why the supplier wants more money
NegotiationResponse: A form that stores our reply strategy and email content

Think of it like filling out a structured form instead of writing on a blank piece of paper.
