Key Components Explained
LangChain Components
What is LangChain?
LangChain is like a toolkit for building AI applications. Instead of writing everything from scratch, it gives you pre-built pieces.
pythonself.llm = AzureChatOpenAI(...)  # This is the AI brain
self.text_splitter = RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(...)  # Cuts long text into smaller pieces
Think of it like building with LEGO blocks:

Each component is a specialized LEGO piece
You connect them together to build something complex
LangChain provides the pieces, you decide how to connect them

The Processing Chain
pythonself.justification_chain = (
    self.justification_analysis_prompt
    | self.llm
    | self.justification_parser
)
This is like an assembly line in a factory:

Prompt (justification_analysis_prompt): Gives the AI specific instructions
LLM (self.llm): The AI processes the information
Parser (justification_parser): Converts AI's response into organized data

The | symbol connects them like pipes - data flows from left to right.
